{
  "_meta": {
    "note": "Occupation catalogue: each job's ISCO-08 codes (official unit groups), the sectors and kinds of company it can work in, and its usual part in a B2B purchase (buyer_role). How many people do each job, their age, sex, earnings and company size all come from data (people.json, isco_within.json, firms.json), not from this file.",
    "buyer_roles": [
      "economic_buyer",
      "champion",
      "technical",
      "security_legal",
      "procurement",
      "end_user",
      "none"
    ],
    "isco08": "isco08: official ISCO-08 unit groups for each job. population: jobs without an ISCO code are counted from another real source (ILO employers, own-account workers, students, retirees, unemployed) or marked unknown. A 2-digit code means the whole sub-major group.",
    "company_types": "Size bands follow published definitions. Small business, mid-market and large enterprise: Gartner IT Glossary (small and midsize business: fewer than 100 employees small, 100-999 midsize; large enterprise 1,000+); the top is the largest employer's headcount (Walmart, about 2.1 million, 2024 annual report), so it means no upper limit. Start-up: a small enterprise in the EU definition (fewer than 50 employees, Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC). Scale-up: OECD-Eurostat high-growth enterprise (at least 10 employees; Eurostat-OECD Manual on Business Demography Statistics, 2007) below the EU large-enterprise line (fewer than 250). Government sizes are not drawn (public-sector share from ILOSTAT)."
  },
